Oxygen Pipeline and Piping Systems — EIGA Doc 13/20 (@cs-eiga: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_7BBE969N5JQJES1KG9AKNBEZBV
European Industrial Gases Association. Oxygen Pipeline and Piping Systems, Doc 13/20, corrected 26 August 2020, revision of 13/12. [Complete 82-file-page publication](https://www.eiga.eu/uploads/documents/DOC013.pdf).

Read the whole technical publication for an oxygen supply study, including material compatibility, cleaning, component selection, fabrication, inspection, commissioning and operation. Use the actual service conditions and domain, then compare other gases rather than transferring oxygen-specific rules indiscriminately.

Title, contents, harmonisation context and notice were inspected on 29 October 2026. The document grants reproduction with acknowledgement of EIGA; it is not labelled a generic CC licence. It explains voluntary technical use and regional regulatory differences, and directs readers to check revisions. Its evidence supports analysis of a supply interface, not a claim that a reader has constructed or qualified a gas installation. No publication is copied here.

